# SPACBR — AUR packages
#
# Per §41-43 of CLAUDE.md: only add an entry when a specific, justified
# need can't be met officially, and note that justification next to
# it. The installer needs exactly one AUR helper (paru) to build these
# — don't add a second.
#
# arc-gtk-theme — the Arc-Dark GTK theme every gtk-2.0/3.0/4.0 config
# and xinitrc's GTK_THEME already assume. Not in the official repos
# (confirmed via archlinux.org/packages). UNVERIFIED against the AUR
# itself — AUR's anti-bot check blocked automated lookup of the exact
# package name/maintenance status. Confirm with `paru -Si arc-gtk-theme`
# before relying on this line; the installer will simply fail loudly
# here if the name is wrong, rather than silently doing nothing.
arc-gtk-theme

# clipmenu — dmenu-driven clipboard history daemon. §28 of CLAUDE.md
# names exactly this as acceptable ("clipboard history through dmenu
# only if useful") as long as it stays lightweight, which clipmenu
# does (small poller, not a heavyweight service). Your previous list
# had "clipmenu-git" — using the stable "clipmenu" name instead per
# §42's "avoid unnecessary -git packages" rule. Also UNVERIFIED
# against the AUR itself for the same anti-bot-check reason as
# arc-gtk-theme above.
# NOTE: adding the package alone does nothing yet — it still needs
# clipmenud started from xinitrc and a dwm keybinding to actually
# browse history. Not wired up here; this is packaging only.
clipmenu

